Above all three are Composition

-simple association example
Association is a relationship between two independent classes where one object uses or interacts with another.
Both objects have their own lifecycle and can exist independently.
Example
class Bank {
    String bankName = "HDFC";
}

class Customer {
    String name;

    Customer(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }

    void openAccount(Bank bank) {
        System.out.println(name + " opened an account in " + bank.bankName);
    }
}

-Aggregation
Aggregation represents a weak ownership relationship. If the container object is destroyed, the contained object still exists.
class Player {
    String name;

    Player(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }
}

class Team {
    Player player;

    Team(Player player) {
        this.player = player;
    }
}

-Composition
Composition represents strong ownership. If the parent object is destroyed, the child object is also destroyed.
Composition is a strong 'has-a' relationship where the parent owns the child object. 
The child object's lifecycle depends on the parent. Typically, the parent creates and manages the child object.

class Engine {
    void start() {
        System.out.println("Engine Started");
    }
}
class Car {
    private Engine engine;
    Car() {
        engine = new Engine();   // Car creates Engine
    }
    void startCar() {
        engine.start();
        System.out.println("Car Started");
    }
}

| Relationship | Meaning                  | Independent Lifecycle? | Example                |
| ------------ | ------------------------ | ---------------------- | ---------------------- |
| Association  | Uses                     | ✅ Yes                  | Student → Teacher      |
| Aggregation  | Has-a (weak ownership)   | ✅ Yes                  | Department → Professor |
| Composition  | Has-a (strong ownership) | ❌ No                   | House → Room           |

Association → Uses
Aggregation → Has-a (can live without the owner)
Composition → Has-a (cannot live without the owner)

